# rotational data for linear air molecules
#
# For use with:  species air.species <sp1 sp2 ...> rotfile air.rot
#
# format: species-ID N theta_rot(s) [sigma]
#   N         = number of rotational temperatures (1 for linear molecules)
#   theta_rot = characteristic rotational temperature (K), from the
#               equilibrium rotational constant B_e (Huber & Herzberg 1979):
#               theta_rot = B_e * hc/kB = B_e[cm^-1] * 1.4387769
#   sigma     = rotational symmetry number (2 for homonuclear diatomics,
#               1 otherwise); used in the partition functions that derive
#               detailed-balance reverse reaction rates.  Optional,
#               default 1.

N2  1 2.88 2
O2  1 2.07 2
NO  1 2.44 1
N2+ 1 2.78 2
O2+ 1 2.43 2
NO+ 1 2.87 1
